{"n": 178, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "178.webp", "text": "12-100\n\nINSTRUCTIONS FOR WORKING ON IGNITION, OME (DIGITAL MOTOR ELECTRONICS) AND\nENGINE ELECTRICAL SYSTEMS\n\nAlways disconnect the battery or unscrew the ground lead on the ground connection point (reer\nright seat) or interrupt power supply for the ignition coil for’any type of work on the electrical\nsystem, charging the battery or welding jobs — dangerous high tension voltage! Dangerous high\ntension voltage in engine and car electrical systems (e.g. on the tachometer),\n\n— The secondary (high tension) side of the ignition system must have a load of at least 4 k-ohms.\n\n— The engine must not be started as long as the distributor cap is removed or the electric lead is\ndisconnected on ignition coil terminal 4.\n\n— Neither shielded capacitors nor test lamps may be connected on terminal 1 of the ignition coil,\n\n— Electric lead of ignition coil terminal 1 must never be connected on ground or 8B + Therefore\nthe terminal 1 lead may not be used to interlock engine starting when service installing a burglar\nalarm system.\n\n— Never disconnect the battery or electric leads on the alternator and starter while the engine is\nrunning.", "words": [["12-100", 0.4483, 0.0318, 0.5471, 0.057], ["INSTRUCTIONS", 0.267, 0.0716, 0.3506, 0.0836], ["FOR", 0.3546, 0.0723, 0.3769, 0.0836], ["WORKING", 0.381, 0.0723, 0.4347, 0.0836], ["ON", 0.4387, 0.0723, 0.4549, 0.0836], ["IGNITION,", 0.459, 0.0723, 0.5137, 0.0855], ["OME", 0.5177, 0.0729, 0.5415, 0.0842], ["(DIGITAL", 0.5461, 0.0729, 0.5978, 0.0849], ["MOTOR", 0.6018, 0.0729, 0.6429, 0.0842], ["ELECTRONICS)", 0.6474, 0.0729, 0.729, 0.0849], ["AND", 0.7335, 0.0736, 0.7579, 0.0849], ["ENGINE", 0.2665, 0.0882, 0.309, 0.0995], ["ELECTRICAL", 0.3141, 0.0882, 0.3845, 0.0995], ["SYSTEMS", 0.388, 0.0889, 0.4387, 0.1001], ["Always", 0.2847, 0.1538, 0.3202, 0.1671], ["disconnect", 0.3232, 0.1538, 0.3749, 0.1651], ["the", 0.3784, 0.1545, 0.3941, 0.1651], ["battery", 0.3972, 0